IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- First Home Super Saver Tax Act 2017 (Cth). Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2017A00133.txt. Seat: the person whose FHSS
-- amounts were released.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `FHSS release` HAS
    -- s 3: tax payable under s 313-60 of the ITAA 1997
    `tax is payable under s 313-60 of the ITAA 1997`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4: a term of the ITAA 1997
    `assessable FHSS released amount`                   IS A NUMBER
    `released on`                                       IS A DATE

§ `Rules`

-- s 2: the Act commenced with Schedule 1 to the Treasury Laws Amendment
-- (Reducing Pressure on Housing Affordability Measures No. 1) Act 2017: on
-- 1 July 2018 (the date is in column 3 of the s 2 table, which s 2(2) says is
-- not part of the Act).
`the Act commenced` MEANS Date 1 7 2018

-- s 3: "First home super saver tax payable under section 313-60 of the Income
-- Tax Assessment Act 1997 by a person is imposed." s 4: "The amount of the
-- first home super saver tax is 20% of the person's assessable FHSS released
-- amount".
@ref ss 2-4
@export default How much first home super saver tax must I pay, under ss 3-4 of the First Home Super Saver Tax Act 2017 (Cth)? 20% of my assessable FHSS released amount, where tax is payable under s 313-60 of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997. NOTHING where no tax is payable under s 313-60 or the release was before the Act commenced on 1 July 2018. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `FHSS release`  @desc Whether tax is payable under s 313-60, the assessable FHSS released amount, and the day of release
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my first home super saver tax for` r MEANS
    IF r's `tax is payable under s 313-60 of the ITAA 1997` AND r's `released on` AT LEAST `the Act commenced`
    THEN JUST (r's `assessable FHSS released amount` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING
